    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Imagine meeting someone away from the counter. Say hello and introduce yourself as Anna with the name expression. Returning to an earlier pattern after another topic lets you retrieve it without copying the previous model.",
      "text_sha256": "50accacd623b51e6d000b706a44c6d38a9a9cf61d820765c08753e8bfd322708",
      "audio_sha256": "0ebb58c00f2159a88af42d02b972f8e47f6c1699ac1cf68bc67b0a87e86c0921",
      "cacheFile": "1c2b3b935aceade3415a9c2dd4146478f00a3ce148273629eb27c1a08801c558.wav",
      "durationS": 14.825
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "Hola. Me llamo Ana.",
      "text_sha256": "65ac6821445e9f9dd5342a85b44fd0316d82605ef05cf048c76841507b7a1582",
      "audio_sha256": "ebd2dc84afdbcee81a3429ef85b384a91f87924155f618c2af6a6a15a4d31619",
      "cacheFile": "0766310931375b8378b06101c4747d4bb5d24e9be9547d0af5f602553c3423f8.wav",
      "durationS": 1.55
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Say I am Anna with the second identity expression. Compare it with the name expression from the previous turn. They share a purpose, but have different openings. Choose the requested opening during the pause.",
      "text_sha256": "7153b60fc67b1bd724ded7938a4aff8367da7e055aafad8dcf4b707429e2d9ce",
      "audio_sha256": "1c9544757fe55aa24585a687a16aca4f6641ba4966185877f1bfa20d2543f67c",
      "cacheFile": "b9b9efa37896f90eca76f8b3997fa6170a70ca58178634a0c5986983c22aec55.wav",
      "durationS": 13.725
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "Soy Ana.",
      "text_sha256": "9aaf960bf4c9ee280f381d5549dfbf034f2df6f7b5f17e314fa4b6964cdcf001",
      "audio_sha256": "1e9507f8eb496e9e7646ec704c0017090fd117e35828bb5574472bfbf693e181",
      "cacheFile": "732b4d6d2d2df9950ca52cbbf0b74e961f2637d0aed23b582f312f833b6932d2.wav",
      "durationS": 0.975
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Finally, say I would like a tea, please. After the model, try the same full request with coffee independently. Replay sections that need practice; a slow successful retrieval is useful progress toward speaking without an immediate example.",
      "text_sha256": "90d407fa47c97d5656f02304b70b9213b7c549587518a3168979d0f69fbaac6f",
      "audio_sha256": "33308baab34c4f395df50af5d6bbe13fbfecb87b49d1c723d910b067f0510c9c",
      "cacheFile": "0e0f739dac3c9daa636f0234112970c0f35600e0c45c36249644d9f885a96e96.wav",
      "durationS": 16.7
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "Quisiera un té, por favor.",
      "text_sha256": "9a3e2b999a4b9af4d1228be05eb8a877e73ba2d15aa449a9a6b1ca088ddf1820",
      "audio_sha256": "48e058b4674a649fd43b47ef1464068febf118b129bfba4c5fd30cd6a17e6151",
      "cacheFile": "d92a7f2efbaa3aa574a9bca845b8cf97e81fb0a13a06f6086d630d26e327886e.wav",
      "durationS": 2.025
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Let's add numbers. One is uno. Two is dos. Three is tres. Four is cuatro. Five is cinco. Listen to the rhythm: uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco. Notice that dos sounds like the English word two, and tres sounds like the English word three. Spanish kept close echoes of the Latin numbers, just like English did.",
      "text_sha256": "3cffff5f7beffd1c7bc10338c97704e82495ceb96c2f1d93101af21e8a1696e2",
      "audio_sha256": "48fc028dbd132b5a0c5840dfbd45b46aab58f58650fd90bdbdd4454fec8a5364",
      "cacheFile": "6aa56bb752a38756a512781d875f79055f9d597809fbd0f7edea203775caa6fa.wav",
      "durationS": 22.275
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "Uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco.",
      "text_sha256": "2194c50b51bd4b9ca8499756623ac61e6fed7a0f29b7d6ecd24e823bd5e59df8",
      "audio_sha256": "56ab8d109700315eeeb7ff2ec397c194c07785607cd7de4a23a9155b970e46fc",
      "cacheFile": "2ba08848c54ab1052ea8f035c235c69de14a0d0f3ba6607fb74afef5adecfcb3.wav",
      "durationS": 2.325
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Think. Someone asks cuántos? — how many? You want to say three coffees. You know coffee is café. You know three is tres. Build it: tres cafés. The s on café makes it plural. One café, two cafés, three cafés. The number stays the same, only the noun changes.",
      "text_sha256": "46283b26f7861bdfd9416603f06bc63729853f265bad00cf5a05f5b7bbcfb12f",
      "audio_sha256": "ab92c9075924183cc52d5d51b00876aa8dc0bef959b613166e36498d87c6b5d9",
      "cacheFile": "ca8b6eb19dd7ca07673d6af2f5a06327242ec1123aa9a5dfd271472b9f22f091.wav",
      "durationS": 18.875
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "Tres cafés.",
      "text_sha256": "7735969a70f5b7e49ea85353c84daf88c0c4efb4b6e0f1bd8cb5825a12594c37",
      "audio_sha256": "f76186ab9c262979382c53240184cbbd14e82b5e867b72207b0162d7d4a02928",
      "cacheFile": "9531b25e1d6ee7b27bef7cdb8ae0fc921d00b9591e56182cfe2867872e7a2eed.wav",
      "durationS": 1.25
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Now time. ¿Qué hora es? means what time is it. The answer starts with son las for most hours. Son las dos means it is two o'clock. For one o'clock, it's singular: es la una. Two onward uses las: son las dos, son las tres. Same number system, just applied to the clock.",
      "text_sha256": "4093dc24a080882859ac3b071874f85a7da67bcd941047522c977c140833e077",
      "audio_sha256": "cdc50b485e744ba4a950a111ff2750cf94ac850b6774879773e2cbe3e0d35450",
      "cacheFile": "eefd4144c5aed81502147d159b4aeaf616372ad78b106ab4a802c896a27c5338.wav",
      "durationS": 19.85
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "es",
      "voice": "ef_dora",
      "text": "¿Qué hora es? Son las tres.",
      "text_sha256": "f1c30f293f31df23a8074ad1273d63d14e17ff99a4a4ce978c4792a80f97c7af",
      "audio_sha256": "f029639306fe78aaa21b78a43e25afbcf9135e4c3e4c434f05916149abbd9374",
      "cacheFile": "437f6c55a23c7f2bdd4d4c53626ed7f9d65e3eb621248b36e1493a0f4ebb5e56.wav",
      "durationS": 1.9
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Think. You have a meeting at four. Son las cuatro. Your friend asks when. Son las cuatro, you say. Simple. Now it's one o'clock — the singular trick. Es la una. That's the only irregular one. After that it's regular.",
      "text_sha256": "252b429b9e3790745d4a76a93421e5a83794a28707aa91040903294937083df8",
      "audio_sha256": "785ed4d9c693fec1470eb216bd969cc363cadacbbff2ab5055c3808dcaacd225",
